title: A Cricket Dictionary
summary: A comic glossary of cricket terms and jargon, illustrated by cartoonist Jeff Hook, decoding a game Dunstan reckoned as unfathomable to the uninitiated as nuclear physics.
---
<p class="lead">Published in 1983 by Sun Books, 'A Cricket Dictionary' opens the run of illustrated comic 'dictionaries' Dunstan wrote through the 1980s, each explaining an Australian sporting or social obsession to outsiders and insiders alike.</p>
<hr>
