  <div class="col-12 col-md-9">
    <h2 class="h4">About the book</h2>
    <p>From the cover: "cricket (crikk-itt in England, criggit in Australia). Like living in igloos, skateboarding and eating tripe, unless taught at birth it remains forever as unfathomable as Nuclear Physics." Dunstan and illustrator Jeff Hook turn the game's terms, rituals and characters into a wry, cartoon-illustrated glossary.</p>
    <p>Published by Sun Books, 1983. ISBN 0-7251-0432-5.</p>
